### Architecture Flow

Client Interface
→ Application/API Layer
→ Business Logic Modules
→ Data Access Layer
→ Database

The response travels back through the application layer to the client interface.

**Note:** This diagram represents a proposed logical architecture. It does not claim that the project currently uses a particular framework, database, API gateway, or microservices deployment.

## 8. Architecture Comparison

| Feature | Layered Architecture | Client-Server Architecture | Microservices Architecture |
|---|---|---|---|
| Main focus | Separation of responsibilities | Communication between clients and servers | Independent business services |
| Structure | Logical layers | Clients and servers | Multiple separate services |
| Complexity | Low to moderate | Low to moderate | Relatively high |
| Deployment | Often deployed as one application | Client and server components | Services can be deployed independently |
| Best fit | Organized application development | Web-based request-response systems | Large or independently scalable systems |

These approaches are not mutually exclusive. A client-server application can use layered architecture, and individual microservices can also contain their own internal layers.

## 9. Industry Mapping: System Architecture Planning

System Architecture Planning identifies the major components of a system, defines their responsibilities, and determines how they communicate and exchange data.

For the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform, architecture planning separates the user interface, application logic, data-access operations, and database responsibilities. The conceptual microservices model also identifies possible future service boundaries.

This planning supports maintainability, controlled growth, and future implementation decisions.

## 10. Observation

Layered architecture helps organize system responsibilities, while client-server architecture explains how clients interact with the application server. Microservices provide an alternative for systems that need independent service deployment and scaling, but they also introduce additional operational complexity.

## 11. Result

A proposed System Architecture Design was prepared for the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform. The report covers layered architecture, client-server architecture, and conceptual microservices, and includes a text-based System Architecture Diagram.

The architecture provides a high-level foundation for future software implementation and system integration.